# Models staged for the model-showcase image by scripts/fetch_models.sh
# (TSV data rows: sha256 <tab> filename <tab> url; # lines are comments).
#
# Zoo rows cover the two compiles whose hashes are proven identical to the
# device copies (cross-checked against the parking-lot / shelf-ops pins):
#   - scdepthv3.hef                              (parking-lot pin)
#   - clip_vit_b_32_image_encoder_nv12.hef       (shelf-ops pin; prompts are
#     self-generated so a fresh device can boot from the zoo artifact)
#
# Vendored exact device artifacts in models/ (no rows here, kept via the
# .gitignore negation). Same-name zoo compiles DIFFER from these — the
# MODEL_CATALOG metadata in main.py (input dims/format, postprocess) was
# validated against the device builds, so do not swap for zoo downloads:
#   - hailo_yolov8n_384_640.hef      640x384 fixed-res compile (same artifact
#                                     as gym-ops; generic zoo yolov8n is 640x640)
#   - yolov5m_vehicles.hef           custom 1-class compile (same as parking-lot)
#   - tiny_yolov4_license_plates.hef license-plate detector (same as parking-lot)
#   - paddle_ocr_v5_mobile_recognition_nv12.hef  plate OCR (same as parking-lot)
#   - linknet_mbv1_ss_dpm_256.hef    device artifact 93.72 2026-09-02, no zoo row
#                                     at v5.3.0/hailo15h
#   - face_landmarks_lite.hef        device artifact 93.72 2026-09-02
#                                     (zoo build hashes differently)
#   - lprnet.hef                     device artifact 93.72 2026-09-02
#                                     (zoo build hashes differently)
#   - paddle_ocr_v5_mobile_detection.hef  device artifact 93.72 2026-09-02
#                                     (zoo build hashes differently)
#
# Deliberately NOT bundled (main.py falls back to the device store):
#   - vit_large.hef                  ~300MB+ classification compile
#   - Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct.hef       GB-scale genai; devices ship it built in
#                                     and _is_available() treats genai as
#                                     always present.
#
# Zoo pinning rationale: v5.3.0/hailo15h matches the device firmware line
# (HailoRT 5.3.0 on HAILO15H). Re-verify with `hailortcli parse-hef` on
# target hardware before bumping.
